# Fleet Dispatcher — Smitty poller: systemd EnvironmentFile.
# Copy to /etc/fleet-dispatcher/smitty-poller.env and `chmod 600` — it holds two
# secrets (a Fleet JWT and the Smitty service token).
# Format: KEY=value, one per line (no `export`, no quotes needed by systemd).

# --- Fleet side (where the poller WRITES, through the ALS JSON:API) ---
# The poller writes mirror rows through Fleet's ALS so LogicBank fires on ingest.
FLEET_API_BASE=http://localhost:5659/api
# A Fleet ALS JWT for a dedicated service account (create one in app_user; give it
# only what it needs). NOTE: ALS JWTs expire — for an unattended poller, either
# mint a long-lived service token or add a re-auth step. Keep this secret.
FLEET_TOKEN=

# --- Smitty side (where the poller READS, scoped to Fleet's customer) ---
# Smitty's ALS JSON:API base. CONFIRM the port with the Smitty team — Smitty's
# app is listed on :8085 (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md), but its JSON:API base may differ.
# The poller's own default is :5655; set the real one here.
SMITTY_API_BASE=http://localhost:8085/api
# The shared service token sent as the X-Service-Token header (integration B.4).
# On the Smitty side this token maps to customer_id='FLEET' and every endpoint is
# filtered to it server-side, so Fleet only ever receives Fleet-owned rows.
SMITTY_SERVICE_TOKEN=
# Fleet's house-customer id on the Smitty side (Smitty response S.3.a). Scopes the
# reads so third-party vehicles never cross the boundary.
SMITTY_CUSTOMER_ID=FLEET
